  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "What is the definition of \\(P(A\\mid B)\\)?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(P(A)\\) divided by \\(P(B)\\)",
    "B": "\\(P(A)\\) plus \\(P(B)\\)",
    "C": "\\(P(A)\\) multiplied by \\(P(B)\\), then plus 1",
    "D": "The probability that \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) both occur, divided by \\(P(B)\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Conditional probability restricts the sample space to the part where \\(B\\) has occurred. When \\(P(B)>0\\), we divide the probability that both events occur by \\(P(B)\\):\n\\[\nP(A\\mid B)=\\frac{P(A\\cap B)}{P(B)}.\n\\]\nThe ratio is undefined when \\(P(B)=0\\). Therefore the correct definition is choice D.",
